summary: platform/linux's epoll reports nothing for an empty pipe, the reading end readable with its 64-bit word once a byte is written and hung up once the writing end closes, refuses a descriptor watched twice with EEXIST and one never watched with ENOENT, and lays its record out as the kernel does, packed on x86-64 alone; SIGUSR1 blocked with rt_sigprocmask and sent to the process does not end it, a non-blocking signalfd is EAGAIN until it comes, epoll reports the signalfd readable, its 128-byte record names the signal, the sender and SI_USER, and the mask is restored
